  "case": "export-025-neutral-successor",
  "clause": "DESIGN R3.3 \u00a714.3 L961; \u00a710.2 L776; \u00a710.2 L801",
  "derivation": "Derived from the JS lot-4 seal (seal.json SHA-256 2182fdfa57e862f50e2c07261dc2864c3e475cd33c249db6d28dd957b76ccddf), case file SHA-256 8cc7301fddd9ffcfb3634de5ac434bce61dfe23bccf079b1bce330e9da9786cd, by parity-sync decision PS-06 (DESIGN \u00a79.4 L723: IO object centres on one row line; RH = max(minHeight, max(object.h + label.h) + 2\u00b7padding), A = max(object.h/2), B = max(object.h/2 + label.h), cy = body.y + max(A, (RH + A \u2212 B)/2), object y = cy \u2212 h/2, one roundEven per coordinate): the inputs are the PS-06 layout of layout-008-neutral-successor (Task_A y 7008 \u2192 8) and the R of render-021-neutral-successor; the PreparedArtifact copies them: renderBinding (layoutDigest, payloadDigest), viewRevision = H({semanticRevision, layoutDigest, themeId, themeDigest, overridesDigest, diStylesDigest, metricsDigest}), the Task_A IR node bounds y 8 and the artifact digest H(ir) of the shared Result/PreparedArtifact report are recomputed; IDs, idMap, entries and capability do not change. The JS seal carries the decided values. Values owned by that seal (harmonization \u00a73; parity sync PS-H19). JS derivation: Complete loss map of the explicitly bound neutral successor: counter origin 0, pages e_0/e_1, nodes in page order then UTF-16 key (Z-page a-first, a-note, z-lane, z-last; A-page a-lane, a-last-page); every occurrence including the lane carries the semantic-type loss of the single when-true capability record (ruleId drawing, unavailable result). Fails against: Exporting without the bound lane, or skipping losses for support occurrences.",
